            <p class="text-sm text-gray-700">
              I am developing <strong>EXD-Net</strong>, an independent
              computational project examining how stored representations respond
              to perturbations in attractor-based memory systems.<br /><br />
              The current implementation uses Hopfield networks to evaluate pattern
              convergence, energy trajectories, and retrieval stability under increasing
              input corruption. Ongoing work explores how destabilization, reweighting,
              and representational drift may extend the model from pattern recovery
              to memory updating and adaptive learning. <br /><br />
              The broader question motivating this project is how internal representations
              form and change in systems while preserving sufficient structure to
              support continuity across time.
            </p>
